{"id":"decorators","title":"Caspien before and after `@inline`","intro":"Measured 4 Oct 2026, one program at a time, before then after, back to back.","edits":["**Compiler:** `@inline` and `@dont(inline)` on a function. `@inline` inlines every call that is safe to inline, even with `function-inlining: off` and past the preset's size and growth limits; the safety rules (no `@async`, no recursion cycle, scalar parameters, ...) still apply. The optimizer reports what it did (`[note] file:line - @inline: f inlined at N call sites`) and warns about calls it could not inline.","**Benchmark programs:** `@inline` on the six helper functions of `nbody_natural_f64` (`length, speedSquared, kinetic, potential, attract, drift`) and on `advance` in `nbody_arr` and `nbody_arr_f64`. Nothing else: in every other optimised program the aggressive preset already inlines every call that matters (checked by listing the calls left in the optimised bytecode), and trying `@inline` where calls did remain (merkletrees) or `@unroll` (hand-unrolled by 4: 3%) gave nothing measurable.","**Stdlib:** `@inline` on `DynamicArray.get / set / setPtr` and `String.charAt / setCharAt`."],"programs":{"nbody":{"Caspien natural f64 · full":{"before":{"time_s":0.684784,"times":[0.700643,0.684784,0.719703],"compile_s":1.792684,"size_bytes":30216,"rss_kb":2120,"ok":true},"after":{"time_s":0.623441,"times":[0.634118,0.639113,0.623441],"compile_s":2.139702,"size_bytes":30040,"rss_kb":1624,"ok":true}},"Caspien plain f64 · full":{"before":{"time_s":0.573684,"times":[0.582149,0.584996,0.573684],"compile_s":1.924523,"size_bytes":25952,"rss_kb":1620,"ok":true},"after":{"time_s":0.584947,"times":[0.592156,0.588073,0.584947],"compile_s":1.931344,"size_bytes":25952,"rss_kb":1620,"ok":true}},"Caspien loop f64 · full":{"before":{"time_s":0.57896,"times":[0.57896,0.582731,0.585522],"compile_s":2.072311,"size_bytes":35816,"rss_kb":1620,"ok":true},"after":{"time_s":0.594788,"times":[0.60086,0.602477,0.594788],"compile_s":2.05